NCMatrix

CMatrix, the scrolling Matrix screen, is by Chris Allegretta (1999 to
2017) and Abishek V Ashok (2017 on), with the CMatrix contributors named
in this repository's history and in README.md: github.com/abishekvashok/cmatrix.
Its thanks list (README.md) names Krisjon Hanson, Bjoern Ganslandt, Adam
Gurno, Garrick West, nemo, John Donahue, Ben Esacove and others from the
early years.

The network display, packets sent and received painted into the rain, is
by Thomas Bloedorn, from his NCMatrix 1.0 (2005), built on CMatrix 1.2a:
http://webpages.charter.net/tux/ncmatrix/ (archived at the Internet
Archive), mirrored at github.com/mayfrost/NCMatrix (the `ncmatrix` remote
here; its one commit is the 1.0 release).

Asciiverse carried Thomas Bloedorn's network display over to current
CMatrix and packaged it for the Asciiverse catalog (see PATCHES.md).

CMatrix is GPL version 3 or later; NCMatrix 1.0 is GPL version 1 or later,
which allows it to be used under version 3. The whole is GPL version 3 or
later (COPYING).
